Task: Pickup and sweep rules (FR3, FR4, FR5)

Summary: new src/game/mission/parkPickup.ts - pure pickup rules with an
internal clock. Drive-over collects the nearest piece within
PICKUP_RADIUS (0.6), at most one per 150ms gulp window (GULP_MIN_MS)
so a cluster lands as a rhythm. sweep() takes every piece within
SWEEP_RADIUS (1.5) in one gulp on a 500ms cadence (SWEEP_MIN_MS).
Collected ids are remembered: a caller may keep passing a stale list
without double-collecting or re-firing completion. complete fires true
only on the call that removes the last outstanding piece (FR5), from
either drive-over or sweep, and never on an already-empty park.

Why: FR3/FR4/FR5 - the rules are pure logic (radius maths, rate
limits, one-shot completion), so they are TDD'd in isolation before
parkMission.ts wires them in Task 3.

